From de8cffd590900d868fe3a5fd41ba1da023a01c97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:22:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AEStreamParser: size AC-3 frames at 32 kHz as A/52 does

An AC-3 syncframe holds 1536 samples. At 32 kHz that is 48 ms, so a
frame is 3 words of 16 bits for each kb/s of its bit rate (ATSC A/52,
table 5.18: 96 words at 32 kb/s, 1920 at 640 kb/s), as at 48 kHz it is 2
words and at 44.1 kHz 320/147. CAEStreamParser::TrySyncAC3() took 4
words for fscod 2, a frame a third longer than it is: the CRC that it
checks then runs into the next frame, no frame passes it, and an AC-3
stream at 32 kHz is never found for passthrough. Kodi's master has the
same line (case 2: framesize = bitRate * 4).

Hades' AudioPresentation.h repeats the table (AC3FrameBytes(), read by
the player information and by the dialogue normalisation of
passthrough): 8 bytes for each kb/s at 32 kHz where A/52 has 6. A frame
read there failed its CRC and gave nothing, so nothing was ever changed
in it; now it is read as at the other two rates.

Found by CroqueMr in the dialogue normalisation of CB1 (pannal/xbmc#144).

Tests: TestAEStreamParser gets AC-3 frames of 32, 192 and 640 kb/s at
48, 44.1 and 32 kHz, each with both CRCs right, fed one per packet and
built with the host FFmpeg 9.0.2 of the build folder for av_crc(): all
are found and handed out at their size; with the code before, the three
at 32 kHz give no frame at all and the others pass. A new
TestAudioPresentationAC3 checks AC3FrameBytes() against table 5.18 and
reads the frames with their dialnorm; it fails with the code before.
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AEStreamInfo.cpp |   4 +-
 .../AudioEngine/Utils/AudioPresentation.h     |   3 +-
 .../AudioEngine/Utils/test/CMakeLists.txt     |   1 +
 .../Utils/test/TestAEStreamParser.cpp         | 101 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../Utils/test/TestAudioPresentationAC3.cpp   |  87 +++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 194 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/test/TestAudioPresentationAC3.cpp

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AEStreamInfo.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AEStreamInfo.cpp
index 2eddda6..0f88c69 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AEStreamInfo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AEStreamInfo.cpp
@@ -366,7 +366,9 @@ bool CAEStreamParser::TrySyncAC3(uint8_t* data,
         framesize = (320 * bitRate / 147 + (frmsizecod & 1 ? 1 : 0));
         break;
       case 2:
-        framesize = bitRate * 4;
+        // 32 kHz: 1536 samples are 48 ms, 3 words of 16 bits for each kb/s (A/52 table 5.18:
+        // 96 words at 32 kb/s); 4 made every frame a third too long, and no frame passed its CRC
+        framesize = bitRate * 3;
         break;
     }
 
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AudioPresentation.h b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AudioPresentation.h
index d3368ac..721a9a1 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AudioPresentation.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/AudioPresentation.h
@@ -262,7 +262,8 @@ inline size_t AC3FrameBytes(unsigned int fscod, unsigned int frmsizecod)
     case 1:
       return (320 * rate / 147 + (frmsizecod & 1)) * 2;
     default:
-      return rate * 8;
+      // 32 kHz: 3 words for each kb/s (A/52 table 5.18: 96 words at 32 kb/s), 6 bytes
+      return rate * 6;
   }
 }
 
